.TH DANBYEQNTEST 1
.SH NAME
danbyeqntest \- test authoring Danby model equations in eqn(7), not hoc(2)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danbyeqntest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Danbyeqntest
takes real physics formulas already living as Limbo in
.IR appl/danby ,
writes each one as an
.IR eqn (7)
string the way a textbook would set it, and checks that
.IR eqn2hoc (2)
plus
.IR hoc (2)
reproduce the SAME real Limbo function's own output \(em not a
synthetic expression chosen to exercise
.IR eqn2hoc (2)'s
grammar (that is
.IR eqn2hoctest (1)'s
job), but the actual model physics this could replace.
.PP
One representative formula per Danby family, each checked against a
real, hand-computed number:
.TP
.B Trajectory
.IR appl/danby/ballistics.b 's
own
.BR acceleration() :
speed
.RI ( "sqrt vx sup 2 + vy sup 2" ),
and both acceleration components (drag and lift, real
.RI ( vx , vy , drag , lift ", " gravity )
values).
.TP
.B Mechanism
.IR appl/danby/pendulum.b 's
gravity term,
.RI \-( g / L )sin\ theta,
at
.IR theta " = 30 degrees - once with theta as a decimal, once written"
.B "PI over 6"
directly in the eqn source, resolving through hoc's own installed
.B PI
constant with no special-casing anywhere in
.IR eqn2hoc (2).
.TP
.B Populationmodel
.IR appl/danby/epidemic.b 's
real SIR terms (infections, recoveries, and their difference) \(em the
same formula
.IR doc/danby-tks-plan.md
already verified as hoc arithmetic, now authored as eqn instead.
.TP
.B Twospecies
.IR appl/danby/ecology.b 's
real Lotka-Volterra predator-prey terms, at that file's own real
default parameters
.RI ( "birth 1.5, predation 2.0, death 0.75" ).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/danbyeqntest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR eqn2hoc (2),
.IR eqn2hoctest (1),
.IR hoc (2)
.SH BUGS
Checks one representative formula per family, not every plugin \(em the
same scope decision
.IR eqn2hoctest (1)
makes for its own syntax coverage. Mechanism's pendulum check omits the
real function's dry-friction/drive terms (a conditional on the sign of
angular velocity, not a pure formula \(em out of scope for eqn the same
way hoc itself has no conditional expression either).
